From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:50:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: report the always-zero
 SMC temperatures as no data

The J604 SMC hwmon node discovers every readable temperature key. 21 of
them (TVMD, TVMm, TVMs, TVm0, TVm2, TVmd, Ta00, Ta04, Ta08, Ta0K, Ta0O,
Ta0R and Tz11-Tz18, Tz1j) read exactly 0.00 C, in the macOS 27.0.1 key
dump and on Linux at idle alike. They are unpopulated slots, and sensors
tools show them as 0 C readings next to the real ones.

Describe them with apple,no-data-below-millicelsius = 1000, as already
done for the GPU placeholder keys, so they report no data. A reading at
or above 1 C still passes, should one of them ever carry a value.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 132 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 132 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 9b96fcb9e7..d244cec244 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
